WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.332 --> 00:00:04.976
It is Sunday evening. There
are four people to feed,

2
00:00:05.065 --> 00:00:08.710
a busy week ahead, and a familiar question:

3
00:00:08.799 --> 00:00:12.354
what are we cooking? Let's
use Forkcast to plan three

4
00:00:12.443 --> 00:00:15.910
dinners, start with what is
already in the kitchen, and

5
00:00:16.088 --> 00:00:18.813
leave with one useful shopping list.

6
00:00:18.873 --> 00:00:21.776
This is an example household,
so you can follow the

7
00:00:21.865 --> 00:00:23.021
whole journey.

8
00:00:43.430 --> 00:00:46.452
First, we need one dependable dinner.

9
00:00:46.897 --> 00:00:51.697
The recipe collection includes real
photographs and the original sources.

10
00:00:51.963 --> 00:00:57.030
We will choose shakshuka. Open
the details, read the ingredients,

11
00:00:57.119 --> 00:01:00.319
and check the source before
adding it to the plan.

12
00:01:00.586 --> 00:01:04.497
You can also search by
ingredient or filter by cuisine.

13
00:01:25.961 --> 00:01:29.250
Before choosing anything else,
let's check the cupboard.

14
00:01:29.694 --> 00:01:33.339
We have a short inventory
note with rice, olive oil,

15
00:01:33.472 --> 00:01:37.694
garlic, and eggs. Instead
of typing every item, we can

16
00:01:37.783 --> 00:01:40.361
ask the image extractor to read the note.

17
00:01:40.894 --> 00:01:45.161
We are using a signed-in Codex
subscription for this demonstration.

18
00:02:10.749 --> 00:02:14.082
The extractor has prepared
the names and quantities.

19
00:02:14.305 --> 00:02:16.438
Nothing has entered the pantry yet.

20
00:02:16.705 --> 00:02:19.727
This is our chance to
correct an amount or discard

21
00:02:19.771 --> 00:02:23.638
an item. Once the note
matches what we actually have,

22
00:02:23.771 --> 00:02:25.727
we save the reviewed items.

23
00:02:25.949 --> 00:02:29.060
Those quantities will reduce
the shopping list later.

24
00:03:02.785 --> 00:03:06.074
Someone in the family saved
a Food Fusion pulao video

25
00:03:06.163 --> 00:03:09.985
for the weekend. Let's bring
its recipe into our collection.

26
00:03:10.341 --> 00:03:14.207
The importer reads the available
description or captions.

27
00:03:14.429 --> 00:03:18.252
A pasted transcript is also
available when the video service

28
00:03:18.341 --> 00:03:22.785
blocks access. The model turns
that material into an editable

29
00:03:22.874 --> 00:03:23.763
draft.

30
00:03:41.793 --> 00:03:43.660
Here is the imported draft.

31
00:03:44.104 --> 00:03:47.526
We can read the ingredient amounts
and instructions, check the

32
00:03:47.571 --> 00:03:50.860
original video, and make changes before saving.

33
00:03:51.304 --> 00:03:53.660
The source stays with the recipe.

34
00:03:53.882 --> 00:03:57.660
Keep the original quantities
visible for review, and adapt the

35
00:03:57.704 --> 00:03:59.926
ingredients to your own household.

36
00:04:23.912 --> 00:04:26.668
The third dinner is a family favorite:

37
00:04:26.756 --> 00:04:31.201
lemon and chickpea rice. Personal
recipes can start from an

38
00:04:31.379 --> 00:04:34.668
empty form, or from a recipe note pasted here.

39
00:04:35.201 --> 00:04:38.579
We will preview our note,
then adjust the instructions.

40
00:04:39.112 --> 00:04:42.756
This recipe belongs to our
local household, so adding it

41
00:04:42.890 --> 00:04:45.779
does not change the shared recipe dataset.

42
00:05:20.992 --> 00:05:24.370
The recipe is saved. If we
cook it differently next

43
00:05:24.459 --> 00:05:26.770
time, we can edit it again.

44
00:05:26.859 --> 00:05:29.614
The ingredients are still
written in the form we will

45
00:05:29.881 --> 00:05:36.192
actually use: rice, cooked chickpeas,
lemon, garlic, olive oil, and

46
00:05:36.236 --> 00:05:40.103
a little salt. Now we have
three real choices for

47
00:05:40.148 --> 00:05:40.903
the week.

48
00:06:11.392 --> 00:06:14.148
Now let's give the assistant a useful job.

49
00:06:14.592 --> 00:06:17.525
Prepare a meal plan with these three recipes.

50
00:06:18.148 --> 00:06:21.525
The assistant can see the
local collection and pantry, so

51
00:06:21.570 --> 00:06:23.792
we can ask in ordinary language.

52
00:06:24.014 --> 00:06:26.503
It prepares the change for review;

53
00:06:26.592 --> 00:06:29.703
asking a question does not
give it permission to change

54
00:06:29.792 --> 00:06:31.392
everything in the kitchen.

55
00:06:44.734 --> 00:06:48.112
The proposed plan lists the
recipes it will include.

56
00:06:48.556 --> 00:06:50.512
Read this before applying it.

57
00:06:51.045 --> 00:06:53.890
We are happy with the choices, so we will apply

58
00:06:53.934 --> 00:06:57.445
the prepared change, then
open the planner to check the

59
00:06:57.534 --> 00:07:01.356
saved result. We can still
edit the name or dates

60
00:07:01.445 --> 00:07:03.578
and share the plan with the family.

61
00:07:45.924 --> 00:07:48.146
This is where the planning pays off.

62
00:07:48.591 --> 00:07:52.591
The active plan becomes one
shopping list, grouped by aisle.

63
00:07:53.035 --> 00:07:56.591
Compatible quantities already
in the pantry are deducted.

64
00:07:57.035 --> 00:08:01.391
We can ask the configured model to
improve ingredient interpretation,

65
00:08:01.480 --> 00:08:05.213
while the app keeps the quantity
calculations and source evidence

66
00:08:05.302 --> 00:08:06.368
explicit.

67
00:08:35.684 --> 00:08:37.906
Take a moment to read the result.

68
00:08:38.173 --> 00:08:41.017
Each item can show the
recipe lines it came from.

69
00:08:41.462 --> 00:08:45.506
Ingredient insights help explain
the names and pantry rules.

70
00:08:45.728 --> 00:08:49.817
Counts, weights, and volumes stay
separate when a conversion would

71
00:08:49.862 --> 00:08:53.728
be a guess. Any uncertain
amount stays visible, so we

72
00:08:53.817 --> 00:08:55.595
can check it before buying.

73
00:09:21.401 --> 00:09:25.312
Let's compare offers from a real
FreshCo flyer, published for

74
00:09:25.445 --> 00:09:30.379
Ontario from October fifteenth to
November eleventh, twenty twenty-six.

75
00:09:30.645 --> 00:09:33.090
The model reads the original page.

76
00:09:33.312 --> 00:09:37.845
We will review four offers,
checking each product, pack size,

77
00:09:38.068 --> 00:09:41.757
price, currency, and expiry date before saving.

78
00:10:42.612 --> 00:10:46.612
Here are recorded offers
from FreshCo and Food Basics.

79
00:10:46.879 --> 00:10:51.056
The comparison buys whole packs
and shows a priced subtotal,

80
00:10:51.190 --> 00:10:54.256
with unpriced ingredients listed separately.

81
00:10:54.390 --> 00:10:58.345
These are dated flyer prices, so
check availability and current

82
00:10:58.434 --> 00:11:03.590
offers before shopping. A separate
location search finds actual mapped

83
00:11:03.679 --> 00:11:05.101
grocery stores.

84
00:11:56.351 --> 00:11:59.640
At the shop, the same household is easy to use

85
00:11:59.684 --> 00:12:03.462
on a phone-sized screen. Open
the active list and check

86
00:12:03.551 --> 00:12:05.595
off what goes into the basket.

87
00:12:05.684 --> 00:12:08.795
We can export a text copy, share it, and save

88
00:12:08.884 --> 00:12:11.107
a shopping snapshot in history.

89
00:12:11.195 --> 00:12:15.107
The saved snapshot remains
useful even after our recipes or

90
00:12:15.195 --> 00:12:16.440
pantry change.

91
00:12:44.272 --> 00:12:47.383
Here is the saved shopping
trip, including the items we

92
00:12:47.472 --> 00:12:51.294
collected. Reopen it to see
what you bought, or share

93
00:12:51.383 --> 00:12:52.716
the list with your household.

94
00:12:53.250 --> 00:12:56.805
The saved snapshot stays in
history when your recipes or

95
00:12:56.894 --> 00:13:00.539
pantry change, so you can
return to this trip later.

96
00:13:18.371 --> 00:13:22.993
One last change: someone
thinks we already have yogurt.

97
00:13:23.082 --> 00:13:25.838
Let's ask the assistant to add it, but stop at

98
00:13:25.927 --> 00:13:29.127
the review. If we have
not checked the fridge, we

99
00:13:29.215 --> 00:13:31.615
should discard the prepared change.

100
00:13:31.704 --> 00:13:35.260
That keeps an uncertain
assumption out of the pantry.

101
00:13:35.304 --> 00:13:38.282
The conversation remains available to revisit.

102
00:14:11.028 --> 00:14:14.050
We started with a busy week and a saved cooking

103
00:14:14.139 --> 00:14:18.317
video. Now we have three
dinners, a checked pantry, an

104
00:14:18.495 --> 00:14:23.650
itemized shopping list, recorded
offers, and a shopping history.

105
00:14:23.695 --> 00:14:28.272
The artificial intelligence helped
read and organize the information, and

106
00:14:28.406 --> 00:14:31.206
we stayed in control of what was saved.

107
00:14:31.428 --> 00:14:34.495
That is a Sunday reset with Forkcast.
